lisa-selfreview:
Pass 1 (lenient, final): approve. Checked CORE-SEC-001 (no token in logs or errors; only the
hash is stored), CORE-SEC-002 (run token only on the six run routes, only for its task/run;
every other route refuses it), CORE-ID-001 (label lookup then a constant-time compare of the
stored hash), CORE-TEST-001/002 (TestRunToken, TestRunTokenLeaseEnd; the other-task case uses
the same agent's second lease so only the run-token check can refuse it).
Deferred should-fix: AuthenticateRun lists leases by label on every call (a scan in the file
store); fine at PoC scale, an index record would make it O(1).

lisa-design:
The run token's hash lives on the Lease record (spec.runTokenHash) with its hex as a label, so
the token dies with the lease record and needs no cleanup of its own. "Its own run" is the open
run of the lease's task (a live lease's task has exactly one), since the lease's run id may not
exist yet when the lease is granted. auth.AgentAuthenticator gained AuthenticateRun so serve's
wiring (Agents: sched) needs no change.
